@extends('layouts.app')

@section('title')
  Components and reuse
@endsection

@section('content')
  <h1>Components and reuse</h1>
  <p>Propel reuses markup in two ways today: layouts, and sections. Components and <code>@@include</code> are planned, but they are not built yet, so they are described at the end of this page.</p>

  <h2>Layouts</h2>
  <p>A layout holds the parts every page shares. It marks the place for each section with <code>@@yield</code>.</p>
<pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-blade">@{{-- resources/views/layouts/app.propel --}}
&lt;main&gt;
  @@yield('content')
&lt;/main</code></pre>
  <p>A page fills the layout by naming the layout with <code>@@extends</code> and writing its sections:</p>
<pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-blade">@@extends('layouts.app')

@@section('content')
  &lt;h1&gt;Posts&lt;/h1&gt;
@@endsection</code></pre>
  <p>One layout serves every page. The sidebar, the header and the asset tags are written once, in the layout.</p>

  <h2>Sections</h2>
  <p>A section is a named piece of a page. Each section appears where the layout yields it. A section must be at the top level of the view, not inside an <code>@@if</code> or a loop.</p>

  <h2>Planned: components and includes</h2>
  <p>The next features for reuse are a component tag, such as <code>&lt;x-card&gt;</code>, that takes attributes and a slot, and <code>@@include</code>, which renders another view in place. Neither exists yet, so the example below is only a sketch of the intended syntax:</p>
<pre class="line-numbers"><code class="language-blade">&lt;x-card title="Hello"&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Card body.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/x-card&gt;

@@include('partials.footer')</code></pre>
  <p>Until they exist, share markup through a layout, or through the shared data described on the <a href="/docs/context">context page</a>.</p>
@endsection
